    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Google Gemma spans 6 versions in the OpenRouter catalog, first released 2024-07-13 and newest on 2026-04-03. All 6 publish open weights, and 2 of the 6 support reasoning. Context windows range from 8192 to 262144 tokens. Inputs cover image, text and video, with text output. Prices vary widely: the newest Gemma 4 26B A4B costs $0.09 per million input and $0.3 output, while Gemma 2 27B costs $0.65 on both sides. Output limits also differ, from 2048 tokens up to 235929. The open weights and low entry prices suit self hosting, experimentation and cost sensitive text or image work. Limits sit in reasoning, which only 2 versions offer, and in the older small context and output ceilings. The newest tiers are the cheapest per token, so older versions look costly by comparison.",
